During testing, the loading nose moved downward at a constant crosshead speed of 2 mm/min, while the applied load ( F ) and mid-span displacement ( δ ) were continuously recorded by the system. The experimental data were acquired using the Trapezium X software integrated with the testing machine. The experimental results were statistically evaluated using the sample standard deviation approach. Based on the force–displacement data, the flexural stress ( σ ) and bending strain ( ε ) were calculated using the following equations: 1 σ = 3 F L 2 b d 2 , ε = 6 D d L 2 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
